        "raw_text": "\n--- Page 272 ---\n150.]\nDISTRIBUTION OF ELEOTRICITY.\n237\n\nLimiting Forms.\n(1) When $\\beta=0$ the surface is the part of the plane of $x z$\nbetween the two branches of the hyperbola whose equation is\nwritten above, (24).\n(2) When $\\beta=F\\left(k^{\\prime}\\right)$ the surface is the part of the plane of $x y$\nwhich is on the outside of the focal ellipse whose equation is\n$$\\frac{x^{2}}{c^{2}}+\\frac{y^{2}}{c^{2}-b^{2}}=1$$\n(25)\n\nThe Ellipsoids.\nFor any given ellipsoid $\\gamma$ is constant. If two ellipsoids, $\\gamma_{1}$\nand $\\gamma_{2}$, be maintained at potentials $V_{1}$ and $V_{2}$, then, for any\npoint $\\gamma$ in the space between them, we have\n$$V=\\frac{\\gamma_{1} V-\\gamma_{2} V_{1}+\\gamma\\left(V_{1}-V_{2}\\right)}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}} .$$\n(26)\nThe surface-density at any point is\n$$\\sigma=-\\frac{1}{4 \\pi} \\frac{V_{1}-V_{2}}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}} \\frac{c p_{3}}{P_{3}}$$\n(27)\nwhere $p_{3}$ is the perpendicular from the centre on the tangent\nplane, and $P_{3}$ is the product of the semi-axes.\nThe whole charge of electricity on either surface is given by\n$$Q_{2}=c \\frac{V_{1}-V_{2}}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}}=-Q_{1},$$\n(28)\nand is finite.\nWhen $\\gamma=F(k)$ the surface of the ellipsoid is at an infinite\ndistance in all directions.\nIf we make $V_{2}=0$ and $\\gamma_{2}=F(k)$, we find for the quantity of\nelectricity on an ellipsoid $\\gamma$ maintained at potential $V$ in an\ninfinitely extended field,\n$$Q=c \\frac{V}{F(k)-\\gamma} .$$\n(29)\nThe limiting form of the ellipsoids occurs when $\\gamma=0$, in which\ncase the surface is the part of the plane of $x y$ within the focal\nellipse, whose equation is written above, (25).\nThe surface-density on either side of the elliptic plate whose\nequation is (25), and whose eccentricity is $k$, is\n$$\\sigma=\\frac{V}{4 \\pi \\sqrt{c^{2}-b^{2}}} \\frac{1}{F(k)} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\frac{a^{2}}{c^{2}}-\\frac{y^{2}}{c^{2}-b^{2}}}},$$\n(30.)\nand its charge is\n$$Q=c \\frac{V}{F(k)} .$$\n(31)\n",
        "mathpix_markdown": "\n--- Page 272 ---\n\n\n\\section*{Limiting Forms.}\n\n(1) When $\\beta=0$ the surface is the part of the plane of $x z$\n between the two branches of the hyperbola whose equation is\n written above, (24).\n\n(2) When $\\beta=F\\left(k^{\\prime}\\right)$ the surface is the part of the plane of $x y$\n which is on the outside of the focal ellipse whose equation is\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{c^{2}}+\\frac{y^{2}}{c^{2}-b^{2}}=1 \\tag{25}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\n\n\\section*{The Ellipsoids.}\n\n\nFor any given ellipsoid $\\gamma$ is constant. If two ellipsoids, $\\gamma_{1}$\n and $\\gamma_{2}$, be maintained at potentials $V_{1}$ and $V_{2}$, then, for any\n point $\\gamma$ in the space between them, we have\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\nV=\\frac{\\gamma_{1} V-\\gamma_{2} V_{1}+\\gamma\\left(V_{1}-V_{2}\\right)}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}} . \\tag{26}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\n\nThe surface-density at any point is\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\n\\sigma=-\\frac{1}{4 \\pi} \\frac{V_{1}-V_{2}}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}} \\frac{c p_{3}}{P_{3}} \\tag{27}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\nwhere $p_{3}$ is the perpendicular from the centre on the tangent\n plane, and $P_{3}$ is the product of the semi-axes.\n\n\nThe whole charge of electricity on either surface is given by\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\nQ_{2}=c \\frac{V_{1}-V_{2}}{\\gamma_{1}-\\gamma_{2}}=-Q_{1}, \\tag{28}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\nand is finite.\n\nWhen $\\gamma=F(k)$ the surface of the ellipsoid is at an infinite\n distance in all directions.\n\n\nIf we make $V_{2}=0$ and $\\gamma_{2}=F(k)$, we find for the quantity of\n electricity on an ellipsoid $\\gamma$ maintained at potential $V$ in an\n infinitely extended field,\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\nQ=c \\frac{V}{F(k)-\\gamma} . \\tag{29}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\n\nThe limiting form of the ellipsoids occurs when $\\gamma=0$, in which\n case the surface is the part of the plane of $x y$ within the focal\n ellipse, whose equation is written above, (25).\n\n\nThe surface-density on either side of the elliptic plate whose\n equation is (25), and whose eccentricity is $k$, is\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\n\\sigma=\\frac{V}{4 \\pi \\sqrt{c^{2}-b^{2}}} \\frac{1}{F(k)} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-\\frac{a^{2}}{c^{2}}-\\frac{y^{2}}{c^{2}-b^{2}}}}, \\tag{30.}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n\nand its charge is\n\n$$\\begin{equation*}\nQ=c \\frac{V}{F(k)} . \\tag{31}\n\\end{equation*}$$\n",
